# Architecture & package layout

Prefer a **shared core** plus **thin platform backends**:

```text
core/                 # 100% shared — traits, state machines, adapters
platform-mac/         # stub / dev HostBackend
platform-linux/       # CI / lab HostBackend
platform-jetson/      # Orin / A-box family (capability detect at runtime)
```

Exact crate names are consumer foundation + ADR. Constitution rule: **business
and reconcile logic live in core**; SoC specifics implement traits only.

## Hard rules

1. **No `#ifdef Orin`** (or equivalent) in core business paths — use traits /
   features selected at build or capability detection after install.
2. **Config absorbs path differences** (e.g. storage layout) — prefer
   profile/config over forked logic trees.
3. Entrypoint stays thin: load config, wire DI, run supervisor loop.
4. Product module maps and cloud schema catalogs are **not** constitution —
   consumer `docs/specification/`.

